<https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/KB/Agent/Ontario.%20Forest%20Protection%20Branch> <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#history> "The Forest Protection Branch was created within the Ontario Department of Lands and Forests in 1960, replacing the Division of Forest Protection. The branch was comprised of the Forest Protection Section and for Air Services Section. In 1969, the Engineering Services Section was also formed as part of the branch. The Forest Protection Branch ceased to exist in 1971. The Forest Protection Section and Air Services Section became part of the Environmental Protection Branch, and the Engineering Services Section became part of the Surveys and Engineering Branch." .
