<https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/KB/Agent/Ontario.%20Trade%20Development%20Branch%20%281993-1996%29> <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#history> "The Trade Development Branch was formed in 1993 in the Ontario Ministry of Economic Development and Trade within the Trade and Investment Marketing Division. It assumed some of the responsibilities of the former Trade and Investment Support Branch. The branch consisted at creation of the Export Services Section, the Americas Section and the Overseas Section. These last two sections assumed some of the responsibilities of the former international offices of the ministry, which were closed in 1993. In 1996 the Trade Development Branch ceased to exist when its functions were assumed by the Ontario International Trade Corporation." .
