<https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/KB/Agent/Ontario%20Telephone%20Services%20Commission> <https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/Schema/Authority/functionNote> "The Ontario Telephone Services Commission was a provincial, quasi- judicial regulatory body responsible for hearing and deciding all applications filed by the industry as well as by the public. The Commission issued orders and directions for the regulation of the thirty independent telephone systems in Ontario, and ensured that rates charged for services were just and reasonable and that efficient and adequate services were provided to the systems customers." .
<https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/KB/VariantAgentName/Ontario.%20Transportation%20and%20Regulation%20Division> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#AgentName> .
<https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/KB/Agent/Ontario.%20Occupational%20Health%20and%20Safety%20Branch> <https://data.archives.gov.on.test.gbad.ca/Schema/Authority/functionNote> "The function of this branch is to coordinate the programs and services that administer the Occupational Health and Safety Act and its regulations. It aims to foster a healthy and safe working environment and to encourage cooperation between employers and workers in identifying and controlling health and safety hazards. The branch operates the following programs: Professional and Specialized Services, Industrial Health and Safety Program, Construction Health and Safety Program, Mining Health and Safety Program, Mine Rescue Program, Regulation Development Unit, Health and Safety Studies Unit (amalgamated with Professional and Specialized Services in 1996-97), Occupational Health Laboratory Services, Materials Testing Laboratory, Radiation Protection Services. The services are provided in the Area, District and Satellite Offices across the province." .
